# Netlify fallback rules.
#
# Every real page is prerendered to its own document, and Netlify serves an existing file
# before it consults this file - so these rules only ever fire for a URL that does not exist.
#
# The 404 on the right-hand side is the status Netlify returns. It matters: a rewrite that
# answered 200 would tell crawlers the mistyped URL is a real page, and the branded NotFound
# content would start competing with the pages it is meant to replace. Unknown URLs are
# deliberately not sent to the homepage either - that loses the address the visitor typed and
# hides the mistake from them.
#
# Locale order is most-specific first, so a bad URL under /hy or /ru answers in that language
# rather than falling through to English.

/hy/*   /hy/not-found/index.html   404
/ru/*   /ru/not-found/index.html   404
/*      /not-found/index.html      404
